  "brief_description": "Far from the soft, rolling sand dunes at many seaside places, those in Wouwerman's painting are craggy with rocks here and there. The stark outline of the broken fence against the sky seems forbidding, and the house up on the left bank, gable end facing us, seems to shut us out.\n\nIndividual parts of the painting listed in this way might make it seem unappealing, but the warm yellows of the softer sand between the rocks and the sensation of the clouds moving away to reveal the dawn light save it from being bleak and uninviting. The two small figures in the water give the picture a playful air that is rare in Wouwerman's dune paintings.",
